Third-party models bundled in extension/public/
-----------------------------------------------

models/face_detection_yunet.onnx
  YuNet face detector, from the OpenCV Model Zoo
  (https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/face_detection_yunet).
  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2020 Shiqi Yu.

tesseract/eng.traineddata.gz
  Tesseract OCR English language data (https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast).
  Apache License 2.0.

models/ui_detector.onnx  — AGPL-3.0
  Our own UI and PII detector, fine-tuned from Ultralytics YOLO11n
  (https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics). Ultralytics licenses YOLO and the
  models trained with it under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0, so this
  model file, and the training code in ml/ that produces it, are distributed under
  AGPL-3.0 rather than Apache-2.0. The complete source needed to reproduce it — the
  synthetic data generator, the training script and its configuration — is
  published in this repository, as AGPL-3.0 requires. Anyone redistributing the
  model, or a product built on it, must do the same or obtain an Ultralytics
  Enterprise licence. Without the file, the extension still runs on its other
  layers (DOM, YuNet, OCR).

Dependencies installed at build time
------------------------------------

The extension and server download their libraries (onnxruntime-web, Tesseract.js,
WXT, FastAPI and others) from npm and PyPI during setup; each is used under its own
licence and none is redistributed in this repository.
